
		WORDSTAR KEYBOARD LAYOUT FOR VEDIT
		----------------------------------

The WordStar layout comes very close for the common cursor movement and
editing functions.  Most of the original WordStar control keys and some of the
newer (Version 4 and later) IBM PC Function keys are emulated.

Major Differences:

1.  <F1> and <Ctrl-J> are the [HELP] keys.  <F10> pops up the menu system.

2.  <F2> performs only [CANCEL], <Ctrl-U> performs {UNDO, Line}.

3.  <Enter> inserts a CR-LF (splits the line) when in insert mode.  <F3>
    always moves the cursor to the next line.

4.  While the Wordstar block functions are closely emulated, it is easier to
    use <F9> - {BLOCK, Set Marker} to set block markers, and <Ctrl-F9> and
    <Alt-F9> to copy and move blocks.

5.  The file save functions that WordStar assigns to <F9> and <F10> are
    available from the [ESCAPE] menu.  <F9> performs block operations, while
    <F10> is [MENU] and <Alt-F10> is [VISUAL EXIT].

6.  Although Wordstar assigns <Home> equivalent to ^QE (top of screen) and
    <End> equivalent to ^QX (end of screen), we have assigned <Home> to 
    [LINE BEGIN] and <End> to [LINE END].


    Note:  [HELP] will first display the keyboard layout listed on the next 
	   page.  However, the screen for "Built-in Keystroke Macros" will not 
	   be entirely correct.  This can be corrected by editing the 
	   beginning of VHELP.HLP (VEDIT PLUS: VVHELP.HLP) which is an
	   explanation of the built-in keystroke macros.


		  KEYBOARD LAYOUT

"+" indicates functions not available on WordStar
"!" indicates functions which operate differently from WordStar

[BACKSPACE]		^H			<Backspace>
[BLOCK COPY]		^K C			<Shft-F8>	<Ctrl-F9>
[BLOCK MOVE]		^K V			<Shft-F7>	<Alt-F9>
[CANCEL]		<F2>
[CURSOR UP]		^E			<Up Arrow>
[CURSOR DOWN]		^X			<Down Arrow>
[CURSOR RIGHT]		^D			<Right Arrow>
[CURSOR LEFT]		^S			<Left Arrow>
[DELETE]		^G			<Del>
[DEL PREV WORD]    +	<Ctrl-Bksp>
[DEL NEXT WORD]		^T			<F6>
[ENTER CTRL]		^P P
[ERASE EOL]	    	^Q Y
[ERASE LINE]		^Y			<F5>
[ESCAPE]	   +	<ESC>
[FORMAT PARA]		^B
[HELP]			^J			<F1>
[INDENT]	   +	<F8>
[INSERT MODE]	   	^V			<Ins>
[LINE BEGIN]	   	^Q S
[LINE END]	   	^Q D
[MENU]		   +	<F10>
[NEXT LINE]	   !	<F3>
[NEXT PARA]	   +	^Q <PgDn>
[NEXT TAB STOP]	   +	^Q --->|		|<---  (Shift --->|)
[NEXT WORD]		^F			<Ctrl-Right Arrow>
[PAGE UP]		^R			<PgUp>
[PAGE DOWN]		^C			<PgDn>
[PREVIOUS PARA]		^Q <PgUp>
[PREVIOUS WORD]		^A			<Ctrl-Left Arrow>
[REPEAT]		^Q Q
[REPEAT LAST]	   +	<Alt-R>
[REPLACE]		^Q A			<Ctrl-F2>
[SCREEN BEGIN]	   	^Q E
[SCREEN END]	   	^Q X
[SCROLL UP]		^W			<Ctrl-PgUp>
[SCROLL DOWN]		^Z			<Ctrl-PgDn>
[SCROLL RIGHT]	   +	^Q <Right Arrow>
[SCROLL LEFT]	   +	^Q <Left Arrow>
[SEARCH]		^Q F			<Ctrl-F1>
[SEARCH AGAIN]		^L			<Ctrl-F3>
[TAB CHARACTER]		--->|
[T-REG COPY]	   +	<Grey +>
[T-REG MOVE]	   +	<Grey ->
[T-REG INSERT]	   +	<Grey *>
[UNDENT]	   +	<F7>
[VISUAL ESCAPE]	   +	Available in ESCAPE menu
[VISUAL EXIT]	   +	<Alt-F10>

Begin of file		^Q R			<Ctrl-Home>
End of file		^Q C			<Ctrl-End>
Begin of block	    	^Q B
End of block	    	^Q K
To specified line	^Q I			<Ctrl-F4>
Start of last find   !	^Q V			(Simulated by {UNDO, Edit})
To Marker 0-9		^Q 0 through ^Q 9

Delete line to left	^Q <Del>
Delete word		^T			<F6>

Mark block begin    	^K B			<Shft-F9>
Mark block end     	^K K			<Shft-F10>
Copy Block	    	^K C			<Shft-F8>
Move Block	    	^K V			<Shft-F7>
Delete block	    	^K Y			<Shft-F5>
Column mode		^K N
Write block to disk	^K W
Set Marker 0-9		^K 0 through ^K 9
Convert block to LC	^K '
Convert block to UC	^K "	

Insert a file from disk		^K R
Run a program/DOS command	^K F
Change logged drive/direc	^K L
Save and resume editing		^K S
Save menu		   !!	^K D
Save and exit window		^K X
Quit without saving		^K Q
Save and Print			<Ctrl-PrtSc>

Set right margin		^O R		<Ctrl-F6>
Set left margin			^O L		<Ctrl-F5>
Justify				^O J
Center line			^O C		<Shft-F2>

Insert date			^P @
Insert time			^P !
Insert Line-Feed		^P J
Insert Form-Feed		^P L
Insert CR-LF			^N

Switch/create edit buffer  +	<F4>
Switch windows		   +	<Alt-F4>
Open (edit) new file	   +    <Alt-N>		(Same buffer)
Open (edit) new file	   +	<Alt-O>		(New buffer, same window)
Open (edit) new file	   +	<Alt-Y>		(New buffer, new window)
Toggle between files	   +	<Alt-T>
Toggle VGA/EGA line mode   +	<Alt-L>
Toggle text colors	   +	<Alt-J>
Start up Compiler Support  +	<Alt-I>

{Block}  Menu	<Alt-B>		{Config} Menu	<Alt-C>
{Edit}   Menu	<Alt-E>		{File}   Menu	<Alt-F>
{Goto}   Menu	<Alt-G>		{Help}   Menu	<Alt-H>
{Misc}   Menu	<Alt-M>		{Print}  Menu	<Alt-P>
{Search} Menu	<Alt-S>		{Window} Menu	<Alt-W>
